# Every env file, not just *.local. `vercel env pull <name>` writes whatever
# filename it is given, and `.env.prod` slipped past the old two-line rule
# straight into a commit. Deny all of them; add an explicit negation if a
# checked-in example file is ever wanted.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.DS_Store

